{"parentUuid":"f45b0c60-a253-4d80-872d-923c138f196b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffeWgoHo1gxKMkGDr4PL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NBGF22Dck4NhgiiQB7C7DN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git status | head -3 && ls && cat spec/capabilities/stop-hook-payload.yaml spec/capabilities/stop-block-continuation.yaml | head -150 && grep -rln \"stop-hook-payload\\|stop-block-continuation\" --include=* . 2>/dev/null | grep -v '^./.git/' | head -30"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5510,"cache_read_input_tokens":44970,"output_tokens":359,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5510},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":359,"cache_read_input_tokens":44970,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5510,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NBGF22Dck4NhgiiQB7C7DN":{"command":"cd /Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30 && git status | head -3 && ls && cat spec/capabilities/stop-hook-payload.yaml spec/capabilities/stop-block-continuation.yaml | head -150 && grep -rln \"stop-hook-payload\\|stop-block-continuation\" --include=* . 2>/dev/null | grep -v '^./.git/' | head -30"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01NBGF22Dck4NhgiiQB7C7DN":{"cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffeWgXfphnrukf62x4qm","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"17b65738-c762-4f77-bed6-3205f3c05d1e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:49:57.640Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"f45b0c60-a253-4d80-872d-923c138f196b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LcK6trLNsvJ6TYsxr12UVU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tYou are one of 31 parallel agents; each takes ONE capability in the repo you are in (a git worktree of sloprail/harness-mocks). Goal: every `pending` cell of your capability's spec file (spec/capabilities/<id>.yaml) becomes real: **supported** (docs + recorded runs of the REAL harness, an adapter in the mock, tests) or **unsupported with evidence**. Recorded runs outrank docs: a run showing the behaviour (even partly) => supported, the gaps listed as `deviations`; a run showing the behaviour absent (whose scenario really attempts it) => `{supported: false, reason: <one line>, runs: [...] and/or docs: [...]}`. Never leave `pending`, never a bare `false`. Do NOT change the capability's `statement` (that needs the user's words) nor other capabilities' cells.\n2\t\n3\tA finished example, already on main: `git show f860ff3` (codex x bash-tool-result): scenario under codex-mock/snapshots/runs/<name>/setup/, captured with the harness's snapshots/capture.sh, cell in the spec file, `// sr:provides <id>/<harness>` adapter marker, `// sr:proves <id>/<harness>` test. Read it first, plus adr/capability-grounding, adr/capability-once, adr/modeled-surface, .sloprail/schemas/capability.cue, and the existing cells and tests of the same harness.\n4\t\n5\tHow things work\n6\t- Real harnesses are installed and logged in: `codex` and `cursor-agent`. Record with `<harness>-mock/snapshots/capture.sh run <name>` (the ONLY writer of snapshots/; hand-authored `setup/` = prompt.txt, hooks.json, hook scripts, optional args/env; read the script's header and the existing runs). It makes real model calls: keep prompts short, and capture only what you need (a few runs). Captures are serialised by a lock per harness; wait for it. `capture.sh doc <url>` freezes a doc page into the MANIFEST (cells cite `https://...#anchor` of a frozen page). Reuse existing runs when they already show the behaviour (cite them), else add new ones; run names are kebab-case; a new run name you create must be unique to your capability (prefix it with the capability id or a clear name) so parallel agents don't collide.\n7\t- Look at what the real harness did (events.jsonl, stream.jsonl, payloads.jsonl, transcript/) before deciding. Your own scenario must really attempt the behaviour; if the harness cannot do it (no such tool/hook/flag), record the attempt and mark the cell unsupported citing that run (and docs if they show it).\n8\t- Supported cell: the mock's adapter (<harness>-mock/) provides it, core behaviour lives once in internal/ (`// sr:capability <id>` already exists there; behaviour that differs per harness is a PARAMETER of core, never a copy). An adapter translates and decides nothing. Mark adapter code `// sr:provides <id>/<harness>`, and add e2e/unit tests marked `// sr:proves <id>/<harness>` (on tests only, in *_test.go) that replay/drive the mock into the recorded situation and assert what the recording shows (or the declared deviation). Unsupported cells have NO markers. `deviations` are `{adr, statement}`: use `adr: modeled-surface` where the mock models less than the harness does (interactive-only things, unimplemented tools/events), and `adr: capability-grounding` where the real harness itself doesn't do a part of the statement.\n9\t- Scope: if modelling the behaviour in the mock is large, model what the recordings show of it and declare the rest as modeled-surface deviations; do not fake behaviour the recordings don't show.\n10\t- CRITICAL for judges: the rules judge every capability that has a marker in any file you touch (whole file). So do NOT edit existing files that carry other capabilities' markers unless unavoidable; prefer NEW files for your adapter code and tests (new Go files must lie in a module home: see the module.yaml files / adr/modules-cover-code; internal/ and *-mock/ code each belongs to exactly one module). If you must touch a file with other markers, expect the judges to also re-judge those pairs and be ready to satisfy them. Keep `file-size` and `layering` ADR limits. Other agents work in parallel on other capabilities; touch only what yours needs; shared core edits should be small, additive, parameterised.\n11\t- Verify: `go build ./... && go vet ./...`, tests of what you touched (`go test -count=1 ./<harness>-mock/... ./internal/... ./tools/...`; e2e suites build the mock themselves), gofmt. Then commit (signed commits are on; message body ends with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`), `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main` (conflicts, e.g. MANIFEST.yaml, are plain merges: keep both sides; if a rebase changes snapshot files, never hand-edit sealed samples), then run the repo's checks: `sr-checks run --base origin/main --head HEAD` (runs judges with a model, ~1-3 min; it caches by content; repeat until it prints no refusals). Read each refusal and fix the cause (a test that doesn't assert what the recording shows, a deviation that is false, a cell not shown by its citations...). A refusal about something clearly pre-existing and unrelated to your change: report it rather than rewriting other capabilities.\n12\t- Merge: `git push -u origin HEAD`, `gh pr create --base main` (title \"<harness>: <id> ...\"; body ends with \"🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\"), wait for CI (`gh pr checks <n> --watch`), and when ALL checks pass: `gh pr merge <n> --squash --admin` (the user authorised admin-merge when CI passes). If main moved meanwhile and CI/verify fails on a stale base, rebase, re-run sr-checks, push --force-with-lease, and retry. Never merge with a failing check.\n13\t- Do not touch other worktrees, never use bare `git stash`, never `cd` out of your worktree.\n14\t\n15\tFinal report (short): per cell: supported/unsupported, runs captured, what you implemented, PR number and merge status, anything left red and why.\n16\t\n17\tCapture gotcha (cursor): the installed `cursor-agent` may be newer (2026.10.01) than snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml's version (2026.09.28), and capture.sh refuses. Do NOT run `capture.sh all`. Instead put the 2026.09.28 build on PATH for the capture: look in `~/.local/share/cursor-agent/versions/` for the directory of that version and prepend it to PATH (`PATH=<dir>:$PATH cursor-mock/snapshots/capture.sh run <name>`; check `cursor-agent --version` prints 2026.09.28 first).\n18\t"}]},"uuid":"7e49a89e-2fc2-449c-9bc4-b781e55030e2","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:50:00.231Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f45b0c60-a253-4d80-872d-923c138f196b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"17b65738-c762-4f77-bed6-3205f3c05d1e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NBGF22Dck4NhgiiQB7C7DN","type":"tool_result","content":"On branch worktree-agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\nCLA.md\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\nadr\nclaude-mock\ncodex-mock\ncursor-mock\ngo.mod\ngo.sum\ninternal\nproposals\nspec\ntools\nstatement: >-\n  A hook fires each time the agent finishes responding. Its payload carries\n  the agent's last message, whether the agent is already continuing because an\n  earlier hook blocked, and the background tasks still running. (What those\n  tasks, and the scheduled wakeups the payload also lists, look like belongs\n  to their own capabilities.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#stop\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#stop-input\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgbash\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#stop\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n  cursor:\n    supported: false\n    reason: cursor-agent in print mode never fires the stop hook (the run configured one logging its payload), so no payload with a last message, continuation flag or background tasks is ever delivered.\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/stop-hook-payload\nstatement: >-\n  When a stop hook blocks, its reason is handed back to the agent, the turn\n  goes on, and the caller sees a single result at the turn's real end. (A stop\n  hook that only gives the agent context, without blocking, is not part of\n  this.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#stop-decision-control\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-2-behavior-per-event\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/cap\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#stop\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n  cursor:\n    supported: false\n    reason: cursor-agent in print mode never fires the stop hook (the run configured one answering with a followup_message), so nothing is handed back and the turn ends once with a single result.\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/stop-block-continuation\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3713a2db-9006-459b-99ce-31a7ea946e97","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:50:00.871Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"17b65738-c762-4f77-bed6-3205f3c05d1e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
