09Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"a4a77692-0116-459b-8dfb-75d8c3262572","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsFY8YKPkLaCtghfKFRoJs","type":"tool_result","content":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.git/sloprail-doc-cache/724881d81f1a9fdb35ea42d4851a11b1f6606bbc6e9d2d05c1e8c466fc25c630.md\n11:- Run a custom validation check when a chat turn stops, enforcing standards\n25:| During a turn                     | `PreToolUse`, `PermissionRequest`, `PostToolUse`, `PreCompact`, `PostCompact`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop` |\n85:  `SubagentStart`, or `Stop`\n163:    \"Stop\": [\n168:            \"command\": \"/usr/bin/python3 \\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.codex/hooks/stop_continue.py\\\"\",\n327:When managed policy and remote hooks are enabled, Work Cloud with local access and dots use admin-managed remote MCP hooks on the cloud orchestrator. Configure `mcp_tool` handlers in Global `requirements.toml`. Work Cloud without local access and personal accounts do not use these enterprise hooks. Command/shell, prompt, and agent handlers; hooks from local configuration, plugins, or local directories; environment-scoped hooks; and `SessionEnd` MCP hooks are not supported with cloud orchestration, even when tools execute locally. When both orchestration and execution are local, existing supported hooks continue to work in local-only Work and Codex threads. Admins can still configure supported managed hooks in Agent Security for those workflows.\n428:| `SubagentStop`      | subagent type          | Values depend on the subagent that stops                     |\n430:| `Stop`              | not supported          | Any configured `matcher` is ignored for this event           |\n485:`UserPromptSubmit`, `SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop`, and `Interrupt` also include\n497:`SubagentStop`, and `Stop` support these shared JSON fields. `SubagentStart`\n499:`continue: false` doesn't stop the subagent:\n503:  \"continue\": true,\n504:  \"stopReason\": \"optional\",\n512:| `continue`       | If `false`, marks that hook run as stopped      |\n513:| `stopReason`     | Recorded as the reason for stopping             |\n517:Exit `0` with no output is treated as success and Codex continues.\n519:`PreToolUse` and `PermissionRequest` support `systemMessage`, but `continue`,\n520:`stopReason`, and `suppressOutput` aren't currently supported for those events.\n522:that hook run as failed, reports the error, and continues the tool call.\n524:`PostToolUse` supports `systemMessage`, `continue: false`, and `stopReason`.\n572:background while Codex continues.\n678:later user turn. If the hook returns `continue: false`, Codex ends the turn\n745:subagent. `continue: false` is parsed for compatibility, but it doesn't stop the\n826:`permissionDecision: \"ask\"`, legacy `decision: \"approve\"`, `continue: false`,\n827:`stopReason`, and `suppressOutput` are parsed but not supported yet. Codex marks\n828:the hook run as failed, reports the error, and continues the tool call.\n834:the request, or decline to decide and let the normal approval prompt continue.\n931:feedback, and continues the model from the hook-provided message.\n935:To stop normal processing of the original tool result after the command has\n936:already run, return `continue: false`. Codex will replace the tool result with\n937:your feedback or stop text and continue from there.\n940:Codex marks the hook run as failed, reports the error, and continues normal\n946:to that nested call. `PreToolUse` can stop the tool before it runs or rewrite\n955:| `PostToolUse` returns `continue: false`                          | Codex uses the hook feedback for the model-visible result, but doesn't reject the nested tool promise. |\n972:matching `PreCompact` hook returns `continue: false`, Codex stops before\n990:matching `PostCompact` hook returns `continue: false`, Codex stops after\n1031:### SubagentStop\n1043:| `stop_hook_active`       | `boolean`        | Whether this subagent was already continued     |\n1046:`SubagentStop` expects JSON on `stdout` when it exits `0`. Plain text output is\n1050:Codex to continue the subagent flow, return:\n1061:If any matching `SubagentStop` hook returns `continue: false`, that takes\n1062:precedence over continuation decisions from other matching `SubagentStop`\n1065:### Stop\n1074:| `stop_hook_active`       | `boolean`        | Whether this turn was already continued by `Stop` |\n1077:`Stop` expects JSON on `stdout` when it exits `0`. Plain text output is invalid\n1093:Codex to continue and automatically creates a new continuation prompt that acts\n1096:If any matching `Stop` hook returns `continue: false`, that takes precedence\n1097:over continuation decisions from other matching `Stop` hooks.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"36c7b70d-ca0f-4ef0-983a-c2e3f492fdd4","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:51:37.446Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a4a77692-0116-459b-8dfb-75d8c3262572","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
