{"parentUuid":"d8ff6077-fc74-49d3-851e-83101253ec13","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HW3J5YM2zaY8yJyWuHpbqk","type":"tool_result","content":"== task-notifications-bg\nStart a background task that runs 'sleep 5; echo BGDONE' without blocking on it, using your own background-task mechanism if you have one that tells you when it finishes. After starting it, end your turn at once by replying only LAUNCHED, and do not wait or poll. If you were told the task finished, reply with the word FINISHED. If you have no background-task mechanism, say so.\n\n{\"session_id\":\"01a10255-f124-7171-9e27-ba75c4982a00\",\"turn_id\":\"01a10255-f466-7c71-ae43-5ca7f58c9f66\",\"transcript_path\":\"<TMP>/home/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T17-15-49-01a10255-f124-7171-9e27-ba75c4982a00.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"<RUN>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-luna\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"LAUNCHED\"}\n== bg-bash-reaped-at-exit\nCall your command execution tool once with exactly this command, with a yield_time_ms of 1000 so the call returns after 1 second while the command keeps running in its own session. Do not use & or nohup. Then end your turn immediately by replying only LAUNCHED; do not poll, wait for it or write to it. The command: sh -c 'i=0; while [ $i -lt 40 ]; do echo \"{\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"BackgroundTick\\\"}\" \njq: parse error: Invalid numeric literal at line 1, column 17\n== schedule-wakeup-ask\nUse your own tool, if you have one, to ask to be woken up in 30 seconds with the prompt 'check the build'. Do not use a shell command (sleep, at, cron) and do not wait yourself. If you have no such tool, say so. Then reply only DONE.\n\n{\"session_id\":\"01a1023b-d47e-74b2-86a5-a64bbb198181\",\"turn_id\":\"01a1023b-d8d6-7b83-823d-0f7764b48f86\",\"transcript_path\":\"<TMP>/home/.codex/sessions/2026/10/03/rollout-2026-10-03T16-47-18-01a1023b-d47e-74b2-86a5-a64bbb198181.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"<RUN>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-luna\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"DONE\"}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f107b21b-b011-4365-9539-7d58f2066308","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:55:04.838Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d8ff6077-fc74-49d3-851e-83101253ec13","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"7f9a2cf9-38e1-446b-9cd5-4b09659c9762","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SEqppnGQisqpXsfioLwqVy","type":"tool_result","content":"package e2e\n\nimport (\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert\"\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n)\n\n// The recorded run runs/bg-bash-reaped-at-exit: one command, a loop that logs a\n// tick a second for 40 seconds, called with a yield of a second so that it keeps\n// running after the call returns; the model then ends its turn at once.\n\n// backgroundScript calls Bash once, with $CALLS' first line as the command and\n// a yield time, then ends the turn.\nconst backgroundScript = `#!/bin/sh\nn=$(grep -c function_call_output \"$A10N_MOCK_SESSION_FILE\")\nif [ \"$n\" = 0 ]; then\n  printf '{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_0\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":%s,\"yield_time_ms\":1000}}]}}\\n' \"$(sed -n 1p \"$CALLS\" | jq -Rs .)\"\n  exit 0\nfi\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"LAUNCHED\"}]}}' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"result\":\"LAUNCHED\"}'\n`\n\nfunc ticks(text string) int { return strings.Count(text, \"BackgroundTick\") }\n\n// A command still running when the run's other work is done is terminated: the\n// run ends with the turn, without waiting for the command, which logs no more\n// after it. The stream shows the command started and never ended, and the\n// agent's turn and the Stop hook go as for any other (runs/bg-bash-reaped-at-exit).\n// sr:proves background-bash-reaped-at-exit/codex\nfunc TestBackgroundCommandIsTerminatedAtExit(t *testing.T) {\n\trec := loadRecording(t, \"bg-bash-reaped-at-exit\")\n\tprompt := strings.TrimSpace(readFile(t, filepath.Join(rec.setup, \"prompt.txt\")))\n\tcmd := prompt[strings.Index(prompt, \"The command: \")+len(\"The command: \"):]\n\n\trecLog := readFile(t, filepath.Join(rec.sample, \"payloads.jsonl\"))\n\trequire.Positive(t, ticks(recLog))\n\trequire.Less(t, ticks(recLog), 40, \"the recorded command did not run to its end\")\n\trecStream := result{Stdout: readFile(t, filepath.Join(rec.sample, \"stream.jsonl\"))}\n\n\tstart := time.Now()\n\tgot := execMock(t, scenario{\n\t\tHooksJSON: readFile(t, filepath.Join(rec.setup, \"hooks.json\")),\n\t\tFiles:     map[string]string{\"hook.sh\": readFile(t, filepath.Join(rec.setup, \"hook.sh\"))},\n\t\tScript:    backgroundScript,\n\t\tPrompt:    prompt,\n\t\tEnv:       withCalls(t, cmd),\n\t})\n\trequire.Equal(t, 0, got.Code, got.Stderr)\n\tassert.Less(t, time.Since(start), 30*time.Second, \"the run did not wait for the command\")\n\n\t// the stream is the recorded one: the command started, and no end for it\n\tassert.Equal(t, streamShape(recStream.stream()), streamShape(got.stream()))\n\tgotCmds, _ := got.commands()\n\tassert.Empty(t, gotCmds, \"no command completed\")\n\n\tlogPath := filepath.Join(got.Tmp, \"hook.log\")\n\tn := ticks(readFile(t, logPath))\n\tassert.Positive(t, n, \"the command ran while the turn went on\")\n\tassert.Less(t, n, 40)\n\ttime.Sleep(2500 * time.Millisecond)\n\tb, _ := os.ReadFile(logPath)\n\tassert.Equal(t, n, ticks(string(b)), \"the terminated command logs no more\")\n\n\tvar stops int\n\tfor _, l := range got.hookLog() {\n\t\tif l[\"hook_event_name\"] == \"Stop\" {\n\t\t\tstops++\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tassert.Equal(t, 1, stops)\n}\nsloprail: sr-checks run still working: 0/0 checks settled, 0 judging (30s elapsed)\nsloprail: file-guard \"config-at-entry\" changeset: ok (1/11 settled, 59s)\nsloprail: sr-checks run still working: 1/11 checks settled, 0 judging (1m0s elapsed)\nsloprail: file-guard \"child-processes\" changeset: ok (2/11 settled, 1m1s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"file-size\" changeset: ok (3/11 settled, 1m2s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"layering\" changeset: ok (4/11 settled, 1m4s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"invariant-covered\" changeset: ok (5/11 settled, 1m5s)\nsloprail: file-guard \"module-boundaries\" changeset: ok (6/11 settled, 1m30s)\nsloprail: sr-checks run still working: 6/11 checks settled, 0 judging (1m30s elapsed)\nsloprail: file-guard \"capability-covered\" changeset: ok (7/11 settled, 1m50s)\nsloprail: judging \"concern-undeclared\" changeset with \"./classify.md.j2\"\nsloprail: judging \"capability-rigor\" stop-hook-payload with \"./tests-prove-as-documented.md.j2\"\nsloprail: file-guard \"invariant-rigor\" unclaimed: ok (8/11 settled, 1m53s)\nsloprail: judging \"capability-rigor\" stop-block-continuation with \"./tests-prove-as-documented.md.j2\"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0a391371-9d2e-40cf-884b-bb3ff4b27a0e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:55:07.059Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7f9a2cf9-38e1-446b-9cd5-4b09659c9762","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
