{"parentUuid":"63ad7ef0-1221-4d7a-8c42-e96d4f7bac1d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0be1bbdf1e9ecd30","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffihHPPZKniMTUgUHmYP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both pairs are fixed and merged in PR #122 (squash, admin, all CI checks passed). The final `sr-checks run --base origin/main --head HEAD` printed no refusals.\n\nI never saw the original findings for either pair. My baseline run printed only progress lines, with no refusal text. Instead I fixed every gap from your brief against the real recordings and the frozen hooks doc, and the judges accepted the result.\n\n**Pair 1: stop-hook-payload/codex**\n- **Recording check:** the real `payloads.jsonl` does carry `last_assistant_message` on every Stop. Across the three Stops of `runs/stops` it is DONE, DONE2, DONE2, with `stop_hook_active` false, true, true and the same `turn_id` throughout. The old test replay stripped these fields, so nothing ever compared them.\n- **New test:** `TestStopPayloadCarriesTheLatestMessageAndWhetherContinuing` in the new `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/stop_records_test.go` replays `stops` and asserts all of that, plus session_id, cwd, transcript_path, model and permission_mode values. It also drives the mock into the `bg-bash-reaped-at-exit` situation.\n- **New recording:** `runs/stop-no-message` shows a reply with no text gives `last_assistant_message: null`. The mock sent `\"\"`, so I fixed the mock to send null (`codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go`).\n- **Cell edit:** the statement mentions background tasks, but the recorded Stop payload has none, even with a command still running. I added the `bg-bash-reaped-at-exit` run and a `capability-grounding` deviation saying so.\n\n**Pair 2: stop-block-continuation/codex**\n- **Strengthened test:** `TestStopBlockHandsItsReasonBackAndTheTurnGoesOn` replays `stops` and `hook-exit-codes`. It asserts the reason comes back as a user-role `hook_prompt` message, one agent message follows each Stop, `stop_hook_active` goes false then true, and there is one `turn.started`/`turn.completed`.\n- **Precedence test and recording:** the doc says `continue:false` outranks block decisions, and no run showed it, so I captured `runs/stop-continue-false` with two Stop hooks (one blocks, one halts). The real harness ended the turn after one Stop and handed nothing back. `TestStopContinueFalseTakesPrecedenceOverABlock` covers it.\n- **Mock fix:** the mock differed, so I fixed it. The precedence rule lives once in core as `turnloop.Resolve` in `internal/turnloop/block.go`, with the codex adapter only passing the parsed halt flag (`codex-mock/internal/hooks/decide.go`).\n- **Removed tests:** the two weak old tests are gone from `capabilities_test.go`.\n\nNo deviations were added to dodge a missing test, and I did not touch either statement. Nothing is left red."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":185,"cache_read_input_tokens":177180,"output_tokens":1015,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":185},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1015,"cache_read_input_tokens":177180,"cache_creation_input_tokens":185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":185,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffihH6nkpY1fALKp45ey","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"aade0405-054c-41fb-9ee0-5b2ab8367d05","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:44:53.749Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/ha